   "design": "The radioactive materials register, kept under the sibling recording task, holds each decay container with its isotope, measured activity and date. It lists the containers whose release date has passed, so the technologist goes straight to them instead of walking the store and reading labels. The technologist enters each item, activity and date straight into the register at the store, so the paper log is not copied. Storing, segregating, measuring, surveying and handing over stay with the technologist under radiation safety rules.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Containers due for release were found by walking the store.",
   "enabler_now": "Registers that compute release dates from half-life and activity.",
   "still_hard": "Mixed waste with several isotopes.",
   "human_edge": "Spotting a leaking vial before it spreads.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Almost nothing changes.",
